Nethack mode enables the use of the ALT key for certain extended 
commands; for example, you can use ALT-c to chat, ALT-o to offer, etc. 
If you don't use "Nethack mode," Windows uses the ALT key for operating 
system-related commands. The list of commands that this enables is on 
pages 15-16 in the Guidebook (where ALT is called the "meta" key).

